# constraints/icebreaker.pcf -- wspr-icebreaker pin constraints
#
# Phase 1: only the 12 MHz clock and the two on-board user LEDs are assigned.
# GPS (PMOD 1A) and RF (PMOD 1B) pins are added by later phases only; do not
# invent pins (AGENTS.md section 2.4, orchestrator plan section 3.1).
#
# SOURCE OF TRUTH (docs/spec.md section 11):
#   Official iCEBreaker example PCF,
#   icebreaker-fpga/icebreaker-examples
#     commit cb9e674cbf0facb84684b02567eb55df3018726b
#     blob   d3097d5bfdf59d7229604ae287df4fb9677b492b
#     file   icebreaker/icebreaker.pcf
#
# Signal names below match the top-level port names in src/top.vhd.
#
#   clk   -> pin 35   official PCF signal CLK    (12 MHz onboard oscillator)
#   led1  -> pin 11   official PCF signal LEDR_N (on-board red   LED, active-low)
#   led2  -> pin 37   official PCF signal LEDG_N (on-board green LED, active-low)

set_io clk  35
set_io led1 11
set_io led2 37
